# ==============================================================================
# Graft: Core / Platform Environment Configuration Template (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
#
# LOCAL RUNS ONLY:
# This file is a reference template for platform-wide (Core) variables on local
# developer and operator workstations.
#   1. Copy this file to '.env' for platform-wide settings:
#        cp .env.example .env
#   2. For engine-specific credentials and tenant coordinates, copy the engine's
#      co-located template (either into its engine folder or merged into '.env'):
#        cp src/graft/engines/<engine>/.env.example src/graft/engines/<engine>/.env
#   3. At startup, Graft loads the root '.env' first and then any
#      'src/graft/engines/*/.env' files without overwriting existing variables.
#   4. All '.env' files are strictly git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
#
# CI/CD (GITHUB ACTIONS) RUNS:
# In automated CI/CD pipelines, do NOT use or commit '.env' files.
# Workflows must source credentials directly from GitHub Repository / Environment
# Secrets via OIDC federation.
# ==============================================================================

# Core CLI log verbosity is controlled via flags (-q / --quiet, -v / --verbose).
# Merge engine-specific variables from src/graft/engines/<engine>/.env.example below
# if you prefer a single root .env file instead of per-engine .env files.

